# Ilva Sarn

A salt-panner's daughter who took the courier's trade because it pays in
coin and the pans pay in credit. She can name every channel between the
tide line and the pan dykes, including the ones that are not on the
Crown's chart, and she has been down the low road at night often enough
to know what the tide does to a person who is not expecting it.

She took the job. Eleven marks of fee, one sealed crate, no questions —
and she is the one who has not told Orson that the fee was eleven marks
and the crate was worth four hundred.

She has been to the [[The Drowned Quarter|Drowned Quarter]] — every part
of it, in daylight, since she was nine years old — and she was the one who
said the wreck was in the wrong channel before anyone else would listen
to her.

> [!secret] Why she has not said anything
> She has worked out, in the hour since, that a courier who is paid eleven
> marks to carry four hundred marks of salt is not a courier. She has not
> worked out what to do about it, and she has decided that the answer is
> to be the last one of the party who admits anything. ^ilva
